title: The Levi Question
subtitle: The congress cannot stop talking about the man who is not on the agenda.
view-if: congress_jena = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and e21_cg_levi_out = 0 and e21_jena_levi_motion = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.e21_cg_levi_out = 1;
Q.e21_backing_levi = (Q.congress_backing == 'luxemburgist') ? 1 : 0;
!}
frequency: 350
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= The Levi Question

[? if levi_in_party = 1 : Paul Levi sits at the end of the Reichstag group's bench, writing. Every speaker who mentions March mentions him. ?][? if levi_in_party = 0 : Paul Levi is in Berlin, editing a paper of his own, and he is all the delegates talk about over dinner. ?] The Left wants him named a renegade from the platform. Zetkin wants him [? if levi_in_party = 1 : back in the Zentrale. ?][? if levi_in_party = 0 : given back his membership book. ?] Most delegates want the question to go away.

- @zetkin: Let Clara Zetkin speak for him.
- @promise: Promise the Left that Levi will be dealt with.
- @refer: Refer the question to the Central Committee.

@zetkin
subtitle: She will bring delegates to Levi's motion. [? if e21_backing_levi = 1 : That is our motion. ?][? if e21_backing_levi = 0 : That is not our motion. ?]
choose-if: comrade_zetkin = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Zetkin is not free to speak.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.luxemburgist_gone != 1) { RG.congress.swayTo('luxemburgist', 0.05 + Math.random() * 0.03); }
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.congress.bitter(2);
!}

Clara Zetkin speaks for an hour about Rosa Luxemburg, about the masses, and about the man who was right about March and said so at the wrong time. [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates move towards Levi's friends.

@promise
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 and e21_backing_levi = 0
subtitle: The Left's delegates vote with us. Levi's friends will find out what was promised.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.08, 'offensive');
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
RG.congress.bitter(2);
!}

In a back room of the Volkshaus, the Zentrale tells Fischer's lieutenants that Levi will not be in the next Zentrale and that his friends will be watched. [+ congress_last_moved +] of the Left's delegates find they can vote for our motion after all.

@refer
subtitle: The hall calms down, and nothing is decided.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.bitter(-3);
Q.unity += 2;
!}

The congress refers the Levi question to the new Central Committee. Nobody is satisfied, and nobody walks out.
